    "explanation": "Leydig cell tumor is a mostly benign non-germ cell tumor that\nmay produce androgens or estrogens and result in precocious\npuberty and gynecomastia.\nThecoma is a sex cord stromal tumor that is mostly benign. It\nmay produce estrogen and present with abnormal uterine\nbleeding in a postmenopausal female.\nSertoli cell tumor is a mostly benign non-germ cell tumor that\nis also called androblastoma.",
