    "explanation": "Fibrocystic change is the most common breast change\nin premenopausal women and is hormone-mediated. It\ntypically presents with vague irregularity or \"lumpiness\" in the\nupper outer quadrant of the breast. On gross examination,\ncysts may appear as blue-dome cysts.\nFibroadenoma: Well-circumscribed, mobile, estrogen-\nsensitive mass; not typically \"lumpy\" or associated with blue-\ndome cysts.\nPhyllodes tumor: Fibroadenoma-like tumor with leaf-like\nprojections; occurs in postmenopausal women.\nIntraductal papilloma: Presents with bloody nipple discharge\nin premenopausal women; not with lumpy breasts or blue-\ndome cysts.",
