    "explanation": "Hypospadias is characterized by the urethral opening on the\ninferior (ventral) surface of the penis due to failure of the\nurethral folds to close.\nIn contrast, epispadias involves an abnormal urethral\nopening on the superior (dorsal) surface and is associated with\nabnormal genital tubercle positioning and bladder exstrophy.\nOther choices:\n(Choice C) Condyloma acuminatum is a benign HPV-related\ngenital wart\n(Choice D) Lymphogranuloma venereum is a sexually\ntransmitted granulomatous infection of lymph nodes caused by\nChlamydia trachomatis serotypes L1-L3.",
