    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "Lobar pneumonia is characterized by consolidation of an\nentire lobe of the lung and is usually bacterial in origin.\nThe most common causative organisms are Streptococcus\npneumoniae (95%) and Klebsiella pneumoniae.\nClassic gross phases of lobar pneumonia\n• Congestion: characterized by congested vessels and\nedema\n• Red hepatization: exudate, neutrophils, and\nhemorrhage fill the alveolar air spaces, resulting in a\nsolid consistency of the lung\n• Gray hepatization: degradation of red cells within the\nexudate\n• Resolution",
