    "explanation": "Measles (rubeola) typically presents with fever, cough,\ncoryza, conjunctivitis, and Koplik spots, followed by a\ndescending maculopapular rash.\nWarthin-Finkeldey cells are giant cells (fused lymphocytes)\nin a background of paracortical hyperplasia seen in\nlymphadenitis caused by rubeola.\nComplications include encephalitis, giant cell pneumonia, and\nSSPE.\nVitamin A lowers morbidity, especially in malnourished\nchildren.",
