    "explanation": "Sjögren syndrome is a chronic condition marked by dry\neyes (keratoconjunctivitis sicca) and dry mouth (xerostomia)\ncaused by immune-mediated damage to the lacrimal and\nsalivary glands.\nDisorders associated with this condition are:\n• Rheumatoid arthritis (most common)\n• SLE\n• Polymyositis\n• Scleroderma\n• Vasculitis\n• Mixed connective tissue disease\n• Thyroiditis\nRheumatoid factor is present in 75% of patients\nwith Sjögren syndrome, regardless of whether or not\ncoexisting rheumatoid arthritis is present. Other serologic\nmarkers of Sjögren syndrome are antibodies directed\nagainst:\n• Ro (SS-A)\n• La (SS-B)\nThe table below shows the association of antibodies with\ndifferent autoimmune disorders by specificity:",
