    "explanation": "Cytomegalovirus (CMV) primarily affects\nimmunocompromised individuals, often causing\natypical pneumonia in transplant patients. It is also\nassociated with:\n• Monospot-negative mononucleosis (in\nimmunocompetent individuals)\n• Esophagitis\n• Colitis\n• AIDS retinitis\nPulmonary infection caused by CMV is characterized by the\ndevelopment of an interstitial mononuclear infiltrate with foci of\nnecrosis accompanied by the typical “owl eye” intranuclear\ninclusions.\n• Monospot-positive mononucleosis is associated with\nEBV\n• Monospot-negative mononucleosis is associated with\nCMV",
