    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Alport syndrome is caused by mutations in type IV collagen,\nleading to hematuria, chronic renal failure, hearing loss,\nand eye disorders such as lens dislocation, posterior\ncataracts, and corneal dystrophy.\nRemember:\n“Can’t see, can’t pee, can’t hear a bee!”\nAlport syndrome is inherited as an X-linked trait in 85% of\ncases, however, autosomal recessive and autosomal\ndominant patterns are also possible, wherein males and\nfemales are equally at risk of developing the full syndrome.\nThe modes of inheritance of select diseases are summarized\nin the table below:",
