    "explanation": "Liver angiosarcoma is a rare type of liver tumor that is\nassociated with exposure to vinyl chloride, which is used to\nmake polyvinyl chloride (PVCs) for use in pipes.\n(Choice A) Exposure to stored grains and nuts which may\ncontain aflatoxins is associated with hepatocellular\ncarcinoma.\n(Choice B) Exposure to smoked foods which contain\nnitrosamines which is associated with the intestinal type of\ngastric cancer.\n(Choice C) Exposure to polychlorinated biphenyls (PCBs), a\nnonpesticide organochlorine, can cause chloracne.\nThe environmental carcinogens and their associated\nconditions are summarized in the table below:",
