    "explanation": "Hepatocellular adenoma is a benign liver tumor that usually\noccurs in young women and is strongly linked to the use of\noral contraceptives and anabolic steroids.\n(Choice A) Rhabdomyosarcoma is a malignant\nmesenchymal tumor with skeletal muscle differentiation. It has\nnot been associated with anabolic steroid use.\n(Choice C) Seminoma is the most common testicular tumor.\nIt has not been associated with anabolic steroid use.\n(Choice D) Papillary thyroid carcinoma (PTC) is the most\ncommon type of thyroid cancer. Histologically, it is\ncharacterized by:\n• Empty-appearing nuclei with central clearing\n(“Orphan Annie” eyes)\n• PsamMoma bodies\n• Nuclear grooves\nPTC has been associated with exposure to ionizing radiation\nRemember: Papi and Moma adopted Orphan Annie",
