    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Hemophilia A is the most common hereditary disease\nassociated with life-threatening bleeding. It results from a\nFactor VIII deficiency.\nThe treatment for Hemophilia A includes:\n• Desmopressin\n• Factor VIII concentrate\n• Emicizumab\nHemophilia A and B are clinically indistinguishable from each\nother since both are:\n• X-linked recessive\n• Prolonged PTT (abnormal intrinsic coagulation\npathway)\n• Normal PT\nHowever, Factor VIII is decreased in hemophilia A,\nwhile Factor IX is decreased in hemophilia B.\nThe hemophilias are summarized in the table below:",
