    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Hodgkin lymphoma refers to a group of lymphoid neoplasms\nthat arise from a single group of nodes with contiguous spread.\nMorphologically, the distinctive feature is the presence of\nReed-Sternberg (RS) cells (neoplastic giant cells). The WHO\nclassification recognizes five subtypes of Hodgkin lymphoma:\n✎ High Yield Links:\nThe table below summarizes the differences between\nHodgkin and non-Hodgkin lymphoma",
