    "explanation": "Reactive arthritis, previously known as Reiter syndrome, is\ncharacterized by a classic triad of:\n• Arthritis\n• Non-gonococcal urethritis or cervicitis\n• Conjunctivitis\nIt is associated with infections by:\n• Shigella\n• Campylobacter\n• coli\n• Salmonella\n• Chlamydia\n• Yersinia\nRemember!\nCan’t see, can’t pee, can’t bend my knee\n✎ High Yield Links:\nHLA-B27 is common in patients with reactive arthritis. This\ngene is also associated with the following:\n• Psoriatic arthritis\n• Ankylosing spondylitis\n• IBD-associated arthritis\n• Reactive arthritis",
