    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Inclusion bodies are aggregates of viral components or\nparticles that can aid in diagnosing certain viral diseases.\nExamples include:\n• CMV (HHV-5) exhibits distinctive intranuclear\ninclusions resembling \"owl eyes.\"\n• Intranuclear eosinophilic Cowdry A inclusions are\nobserved in the case of HSV-1, HSV-2, and VZV.\n• Negri bodies of rabies: Eosinophilic inclusion bodies\nin cytoplasm of hippocampal and cerebellar neurons",
