    "explanation": "Endocarditis caused by Streptococcus sanguinis involves\nthe production of dextrans, which promote biofilm formation.\nThis biofilm facilitates the adherence of fibrin-platelet\naggregates to damaged heart valves, leading to vegetation\ndevelopment and infection.",
