    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Lemierre syndrome is a disease caused by Fusobacterium\nnecrophorum. It is characterized by:\n• Infection of the lateral pharyngeal space\n• Septic jugular vein thrombosis\nCommon anaerobes that may cause head and neck\nabscesses are:\n• Prevotella spp.\n• Porphyromonas spp.\n• Staphylococcus aureus\n• Streptococcus pyogenes\nAnaerobes that may cause abdominal abscesses are:\n• Peptostreptococcus spp.\n• Clostridium spp.\n• Bacteroides fragilis\n• Escherichia coli",
