    "subject": "pathology",
    "originalNumber": 59,
    "stem": "Situation 2 - A 60-year old male, oftentimes develop epigastric pain, nausea and vomiting. He decided to consult his doctor because of the said symptoms. The doctor diagnosed him as having ‘acute gastritis’ and requested for a CBC. The complete blood count results showed absence of neutrophils. The better diagnostic term applied is ?",
