    "id": "superexam-pathology-0010",
    "subject": "pathology",
    "originalNumber": 10,
    "stem": "Pneumoconiosis refers to nonneoplastic lung\nreaction to inhalation of mineral dusts\nencountered in the work place. Which\npneumoconiosis is characterized by discrete\npale to blackened nodules in the upper zones of\nthe lungs. Radiographically it presents as\neggshell calcifications. This disease may be\nprogressive even if patient is no longer exposed\nand it has also been associated with increased\nsusceptibility to PTB.",
