    "id": "superexam-pathology-0037",
    "subject": "pathology",
    "originalNumber": 37,
    "stem": "A 45-year-old woman presents to her primary\ncare physician with jaundice, pruritus, and\nperiocular and intradigital xanthomas. Her\nlaboratory results indicate a significantly\nincreased alkaline phosphatase as well as a\npositive test for antimitochondrial antibodies.\nThe most likely cause of her symptoms is",
