    "subject": "pathology",
    "originalNumber": 38,
    "stem": "The chest radiograph of a 23-year-old medical\nstudent reveals a calcified cavitary pulmonary\nlesion. The tuberculin test is positive, but\nsputum smears and cultures are negative for\nMycobacterium tuberculosis. A presumptive\ndiagnosis of secondary tuberculosis is made. If\nfurther studies, including a biopsy, were\nperformed, which of the following\nfindings would justify the diagnosis of\nsecondary tuberculosis, as contrasted to\nprimary tuberculosis?",
