    "subject": "pathology",
    "originalNumber": 111,
    "stem": "A 59 y/o male, received a blood group identical\nliving unrelated kidney graft. During surgery no\nabnormalities occurred. Four hours after the\ntransplantation, it was noted that diuresis\nsuddenly decreased. Upon repeat laparotomy\nthe transplanted kidney showed signs of\nhyperacute rejection and had to be removed.\nWhich pathological examination findings are\nconsistent with hyperacute rejection?",
