    "id": "superexam-pathology-0231",
    "subject": "pathology",
    "originalNumber": 231,
    "stem": "An 18 yo female patient presents with chronic\nepigastric pain associated with weight loss,\ndiarrhea, and peripheral edema. Upon\nendoscopy, menetrier disease was given as a\ndiagnosis. Which of the following is true\nregarding the diagnosis?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "there is an irregular enlargement of the\ngastric rugal folds secondary to hyperplasia of\ngastric connective tissue"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "associated with excessive secretion of\nplatelet derived growth factor"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "it is a progressive unremmittng condition\nhowever no risk for gastric adenocarcinoma"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "characterized by hyperplasia of foveolar\nmucous neck cells"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "all of the above"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "Menetrier disease is characterized by diffuse\nhyperplasia of the foveolar epithelium of the body and\nfundus of the stomach. It is secondary to proliferation\nof mucous neck cells and not the gastric connective\ntissue. The hyperplasia is secondary to the excessive\nsecretion of TGF alpha. although it is a self limiting\ncondition, it has an increased risk for the development\nof gastric adenocarcinoma.",
