    "id": "superexam-pathology-0409",
    "subject": "pathology",
    "originalNumber": 409,
    "stem": "A 34 year old man diagnosed as having type II\ndiabetes mellitus. Laboratory evaluation of his\nserum also finds hypertriglyceridemia, which is\ndue to his diabetes. The most common type of\nsecondary hyperlipidemia associated\nwith diabetes mellitus is characterized by\nelevated serum levels of which one of the\nfollowing substances?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Chylomicrons"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "High-density lipoproteins"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Intermediate-density lipoproteins"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Low-density lipoproteins"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "Very-low-density lipoproteins"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "E",
    "explanation": "The reason for this is that with decreased levels of\ninsulin with diabetes mellitus there is increased\nmobilization of free fatty acids from adipose tissue\n(increased lipolysis). This increases delivery of free\nfatty acids to the liver, which increases production and\nsecretion of VLDL by the liver.",
