    "explanation": "A subarachnoid hemorrhage is a bleeding into the\nsubarachnoid space, the area between the arachnoid\nmembrane and the pia mater surrounding the brain.\nThis may occur spontaneously, usually from a\nruptured cerebral aneurysm, or may result from head\ninjury. Symtpoms of SAH include a severe headache\nwith a rapid onset (thunderclap headache), vomiting,\nconfusion or a lowered level of consciousness, and\nsometimes seizures.",
