    "explanation": "Charcot-Leyden crystals are collections of crystalloid\nmade up of eosinophil lysophospholipase binding\nprotein called galectin-10. Curshmann spirals are\nmucus plugs containing whorls of shed epithelium.\nThese result from mucus plugging in subepithelial\nmucus gland ducts or bronchioles which later become\nextruded.",
