    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "this is a case of acute lymphoblastic leukemia, the\nmost common cancer of children. It has hypercellular\nmarrow packed with lymphoblasts - immature T or B\ncells. It is MPO-negative, PAS positive, TDT and CALLA\npositive. It may spread to the CNS and testes. It is the\nmost responsive to chemotherapy, and the primary\ndrug used is asparaginase..",
