    "stem": "A 27-year-old woman comes to the physician\nbecause of a 3-week history of fever, night\nsweats, rash on both legs, nonproductive cough,\nand pain and swelling in her wrists and knees.\nShe has not had weight loss. Her temperature is\n37.7 C (99.8 F), blood pressure is 110/70 mm\nHg, pulse is 96/min, and respirations are\n14/min. The lungs are clear to auscultation.\nCardiac examination shows no abnormalities.\nThere is swelling and warmth over the wrists\nand knees bilaterally and tender red nodules on\nthe anterior surface of both lower extremities.\nAn x-ray film of the chest shows bilateral hilar\nfullness. Which of the following is the most\nlikely diagnosis?",
