    "subject": "pathology",
    "originalNumber": 600,
    "stem": "A 21-year-old male presents with a testicular\nmass. Surgical resection of the mass was done\nand microscopic examination of the mass\nshowed lace-like network of medium-sized\ncuboidal cells and Schiller-Duval bodies. Which\nof the following substances is most likely to be\nincreased in this patient’s serum as a result of\nbeing secreted from the cells of this tumor?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Acid phosphatase"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Alpha-fetoprotein"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Alkaline phosphatase"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Human chorionic gonadotropin"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "Lactate dehydrogenase"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "Germ cell tumors of the testis often secrete enzymes\nor polypeptide hormones, examples of which include\nα-fetoprotein (AFP) and human chorionic\ngonadotropin (hCG). AFP is synthesized by the fetal\ngut, liver, and yolk sac. It may be secreted by either\nyolk sac tumors (endodermal sinus tumors) or\nembryonal carcinomas. AFP may also be secreted by\nliver cell carcinomas.",
