    "id": "superexam-pathology-0686",
    "subject": "pathology",
    "originalNumber": 686,
    "stem": "In the third trimester of pregnancy, a 28 yo\nwoman discovers a lump in her right breast.\nHer physician palpates a 2-cm, discrete, freely\nmovable mass beneath the nipple. After\ndelivery of a term infant, the mass appears to\ndecrease slightly in size. The infant breast-feeds\nwithout difficulty. This breast lesion is most\nlikely to be a (an)",
