    "stem": "A 30 yr-old woman presents to her physician\ncomplaining of a recent nodular growth on her\nleft neck. Further history reveals a 16-lbs\nweight loss and intermittent fevers over the\npast3-6 months. Physical examination reveals\nthe presence of a firm, mobile, non-tender, 2.5\ncm lower cervical lymph node, left neck. A\nbiopsy is performed and pathology report\nindicates the presence of large cells with\nmultilobate nuclei, abundant pale cytoplasm\nand significant band of sclerosis.\nImmunohistochemistry is positive for the\npresence of CD15 and CD30 cell markers. These\nfindings are most consistent with which of the\nfollowing neoplasms?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "HodgkinLymphoma"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Lymphoplasmacytic lymphoma"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Mantle zone lymphoma"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "Mycosis fungoides"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "Answer: B\nFindings are consistent with nodular sclerosing HL,\nmost common type (65-75%); cells described pertain\nto Reed-Sternberg cells.",
